  "name": "video-editing",
  "description": "Edit any video by conversation. Transcribe, cut, color grade, generate overlay animations, burn subtitles — for talking heads, montages, tutorials, travel, interviews. No presets, no menus. Ask questions, confirm the plan, execute, iterate, persist. Production-correctness rules are hard; everything else is artistic freedom. Use when the user wants to \"edit a video,\" \"cut footage,\" \"make a launch video,\" \"burn captions,\" \"add subtitles,\" \"color grade,\" or process raw video files. Wraps browser-use/video-use. Requires ffmpeg + uv and one transcription backend: ElevenLabs Scribe (preferred — verbatim, diarization, audio events) OR local mlx-whisper on Apple Silicon (free, offline, no diarization). Auto-selects Scribe if `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` is set, otherwise falls back to mlx-whisper.",
